---
import '../styles/global.css'
---
<section class="pt-0 pb-[68px]">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5">
        <div class="text-center" data-anim>
          <div class="text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-red mb-3.5">Common questions</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-[38px] font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3.5">Frequently Asked <em class="not-italic text-red">Questions</em></h2>
          <p class="max-w-[58ch] mx-auto mb-10 text-text-dim text-[16.5px]">&nbsp;</p>
        </div>

        <div class="max-w-[720px] mx-auto space-y-2.5">
          <details class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom group" data-anim style="--d:0.08s">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer p-[17px_20px] font-bold text-[15px] list-none flex justify-between gap-3.5 after:content-['+'] after:text-red after:text-xl after:font-black group-open:after:content-['–']">How long does migration really take?</summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-[17px] text-[14.5px] text-text-dim">Under one week. The Quivr team handles the move from Redtail, Wealthbox, spreadsheets, or any other system, with clients, notes, tasks, and history included.</div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom group" data-anim style="--d:0.12s">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer p-[17px_20px] font-bold text-[15px] list-none flex justify-between gap-3.5 after:content-['+'] after:text-red after:text-xl after:font-black group-open:after:content-['–']">What does "built on Salesforce" mean for me?</summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-[17px] text-[14.5px] text-text-dim">Institutional-grade infrastructure, security, and reliability, with none of the Salesforce configuration burden. Quivr is the planner-ready layer on top.</div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom group" data-anim style="--d:0.16s">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer p-[17px_20px] font-bold text-[15px] list-none flex justify-between gap-3.5 after:content-['+'] after:text-red after:text-xl after:font-black group-open:after:content-['–']">What happens after I submit the form?</summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-[17px] text-[14.5px] text-text-dim">You'll book a short intro call. We look at your current CRM and show you specifically where you'd get hours back. No pressure, no obligation.</div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom group" data-anim style="--d:0.20s">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer p-[17px_20px] font-bold text-[15px] list-none flex justify-between gap-3.5 after:content-['+'] after:text-red after:text-xl after:font-black group-open:after:content-['–']">Is my client data safe?</summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-[17px] text-[14.5px] text-text-dim">Yes. Quivr runs on Salesforce's security and compliance infrastructure, the same platform trusted by the largest financial institutions.</div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom group" data-anim style="--d:0.24s">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer p-[17px_20px] font-bold text-[15px] list-none flex justify-between gap-3.5 after:content-['+'] after:text-red after:text-xl after:font-black group-open:after:content-['–']">What if my current data is a mess?</summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-[17px] text-[14.5px] text-text-dim">Common, and handled. Cleanup and de-duplication are part of the guided migration, so you start clean instead of importing chaos.</div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white border border-line rounded-custom group" data-anim style="--d:0.28s">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer p-[17px_20px] font-bold text-[15px] list-none flex justify-between gap-3.5 after:content-['+'] after:text-red after:text-xl after:font-black group-open:after:content-['–']">What about pricing?</summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-[17px] text-[14.5px] text-text-dim">Pricing depends on team size and setup. The intro call covers it in the first few minutes so there are no surprises.</div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>